body:
This updates the v7 statement dashboard around session management and export behavior. It makes file-level actions easier to manage in-place, de-emphasizes debug-only surfaces, and adds a first-class choice between combined and per-file downloads.

- **Session controls**
  - Moved the sidebar `Start Over` action into the `Jump to File` section so file/session actions live together.
  - Added a per-file remove action (`x`) in the file list to drop a PDF from the current session without resetting the full batch.
  - Centralized empty-session teardown so removing the last file clears rendered data, counters, file list, and tab state consistently.

- **File list / navigation**
  - Switched file-card actions to explicit DOM handlers instead of inline HTML wiring.
  - Assigned stable per-session file IDs so jump, remove, and export actions work correctly even when filenames repeat.

- **Debug surfaces**
  - Reframed `Raw Feed` and `Filters Log` as secondary/debug tabs with subtler styling and explicit debug labeling.
  - Added accessible labels so the debug distinction is available to screen-reader users as well.

- **Export behavior**
  - Added an export scope selector for `Combined` vs `Separate files`.
  - Separate export now produces one CSV/XLSX per source file with stable disambiguated filenames.
  - When `Separate files` is selected, unsupported delivery methods are constrained up front so multi-file export uses the reliable blob download path.

- **Accessibility / UX polish**
  - Added an explicit accessible label to the export scope selector.
  - Refreshed dynamic export button icons/labels when scope changes so the UI stays in sync with the selected mode.

```js
function getDownloadScope() {
    const scopeSelect = elements.downloadScope();
    return scopeSelect ? scopeSelect.value : 'combined';
}

function syncDownloadMethodForScope() {
    const separateMode = getDownloadScope() === 'separate';
    Array.from(elements.downloadMethod().options).forEach(option => {
        option.disabled = separateMode && option.value !== 'blob';
    });
}
```
